  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-216712",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We take each term of the first binomial and multiply it by the second binomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8y+1)(2y+5) & = \\\\ 8y(2y+5)+1(2y+5) & = \\\\ 16{y}^{2}+40y+2y+5 & = \\\\ 16{y}^{2}+42y+5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
